---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + "/";
---
<Layout title="Museum of Flight — Rahul Jain">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href={base + "origins/"}>&larr; Origins</a>
    <h1 class="page-title">Museum of Flight — Museum Apprentice Program</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">Four-year apprenticeship</p>
    <section>
      <p class="blurb">
        Over four years in the Museum Apprentice Program, I designed models and taught aerospace concepts
        to elementary school students. It was my first real exposure to a problem I still work on today
        in a very different form: taking something technically dense and finding the version of it that
        actually lands for someone with zero background.
      </p>
      <p class="blurb">
        The parallel to my current work is closer than it sounds — the same instinct that made me think
        about how to explain lift and thrust to an eight-year-old is the one I use now when I'm turning a
        data pipeline into a KPI an executive can act on without needing to understand the pipeline
        itself.
      </p>
      <div class="stub-note">Have more specifics — a particular model you built, a lesson that landed especially well, exact dates? Send them over and I'll add them.</div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
